Spec: ContextTenantScript

Platform: Rhai script library (vynil-core 0.7.7 engine)

Purpose:
  The shipped `context_tenant` slot of ./context.rhai: turns the freshly minted
    `tenant` map into the working namespace view the install/backup/render lanes
    read. The offline half defaults `use_backup` to `false`, copies `ha` from the
    cluster profile, aliases the map under `namespace`, and rewrites `name` to the
    instance namespace; the live half then overlays the `vynil.solidite.fr/`-prefixed
    annotations of the real @Namespace object, JSON-decoding each value. Mutates the
    received map in place and returns it.

Exposes:
  @template(@instance, @context) — offline half, invoked via @import_template by
    the orchestrator slot; touches NO cluster object.
  @run(@instance, @context) — live half, invoked via @import_run: runs the
    template half by DIRECT call (`template(instance, context)`, not through the
    shim), then does the annotation read.
  No other @fn; these two match @ENTRY_POINT_FUNCTIONS.

Accepts:
  @instance — read only for `metadata.namespace` (typed @TenantInstance @Dynamic
    on the live halves, the synthesized `#{metadata: {name, namespace}}` map
    offline — callers frozen in /agent/src/tenant/install.sdd,
    /agent/src/tenant/delete.sdd, /agent/src/template/tenant.sdd).
  @context — the running context as handed by ./context.sdd slot 4/5: requires a
    `tenant` map (the orchestrator always mints it before this slot) and reads
    `cluster.ha`. No `args`.

Returns:
  The SAME mutated map (Rhai maps are by reference — the orchestrator's map-guard
    then rebinds to the very same object, `namespace` and `tenant` become one map,
    not a copy). After @template: `tenant.use_backup` `false` (@bool),
    `tenant.ha` = the `cluster.ha` value, `context["namespace"]` aliasing it, and
    `name` = `instance.metadata.namespace` — overwriting the template-lane `client`
    placeholder AND the run-lane `get_tenant_name()` label value alike. After the
    live @run additionally: zero or more overlay keys, each stored under the
    annotation key without the `vynil.solidite.fr/` prefix (`ssl` for
    `vynil.solidite.fr/ssl`), as the @json_decode of the annotation string.

Raises:
  Zero @throw of its own. Unguarded reads: `context.cluster.ha` and
    `context.tenant[...]` — a context replaced earlier without those keys raises
    the interpreter error here and aborts the lane (the orchestrator's guard
    cannot protect its own later slot). Guarded: the whole namespace read and
    the overlay walk (`try`/`catch` — @log_warn verbatim for a string error, else
    @json_encode), and one inner catch per @json_decode.

Handles:
  Namespace absent, unreadable, or `metadata.namespace` landing `()` — outer catch
    logs the warning and the run returns with only the template-half defaults.
  `metadata.annotations` not a map — the overlay and the use_backup re-check are
    skipped entirely, defaults stand.
  Annotation value not valid JSON — inner catch warns, that one key is omitted:
    overlay values must be JSON-encoded scalars (`"8080"`, `true`), not raw text.
  Overlay key colliding with a minted key (e.g. annotation
    `vynil.solidite.fr/use_backup` or `.../name`) — it writes through the alias
    into the shared map like any key; the final use_backup re-check cannot undo
    a non-bool write (Tasks).

Must:
  Run the offline half in exactly this order: set `context.tenant` `use_backup`
    to `false`; set its `ha` to `context.cluster.ha`; alias
    `context["namespace"] = context.tenant`; then set `namespace["name"]` to
    `instance.metadata.namespace`; return `context`.
  Run the live half after the template half: @k8s_resource("Namespace").@get of
    the instance namespace, iterate the annotation keys starting with prefix
    `vynil.solidite.fr/`, strip the prefix from the candidate key (value-semantic
    @remove on a copy), store @json_decode(value) under that key.
  Keep the alias a reference, not a copy: every later mutation is visible through
    both `namespace` and `tenant`, and this is the mechanism by which the
    orchestrator's Returns promise `namespace.use_backup`/`namespace.ha` for
    ./install.rhai and ./../lib/backup_context.rhai.
  Run the use_backup re-check last: when `type_of` of
    `context.namespace.use_backup` is not bool, reassign it from
    `context.tenant.use_backup`.

Must not:
  Call any @k8s_resource in the @template half — the offline lane of
    /agent/src/template/tenant.sdd stays cluster-free only while this half keeps
    zero engine reads beyond properties.

Depends on:
  ./context.rhai — sole caller (slot contract in ./context.sdd).
  wynil-core 0.7.7 script surface (registrars behind /common/src/rhaihandler.sdd):
    @k8s_resource("Namespace").@get, @json_decode, @json_encode, @log_warn,
    @type_of, string @keys()/@starts_with/@remove.

References:
  ./../../../common/src/instancetenant.sdd — same `vynil.solidite.fr/` domain is
    the tenant LABEL key there; annotations read here are an independent channel.
  ./../service/context_service.sdd — the service-kind twin slot: it builds its
    `namespace` block independently of this file, no shared code.

Scenario: offline half materializes the default namespace view
  Given the template-lane context with `tenant` placeholder `client` and profile
    `cluster.ha` `false`, synthesized instance namespace `team-a`
  When @template(instance, context) runs
  Then `tenant.use_backup` is the bool `false`, `ha` `false`, `name` `team-a`
    (the `client` placeholder erased), `namespace` and `tenant` are the same map,
    and no cluster call was made
  No mapped test

Scenario: live half overlays prefixed annotations
  Given @Namespace `team-a` annotated `vynil.solidite.fr/ssl: "true"` and
    `vynil.solidite.fr/note: not-json` (invalid JSON)
  When @run(instance, context) runs
  Then `namespace["ssl"]` is the bool `true`, `note` is absent with a @log_warn
    naming the decode failure, non-prefixed annotations are ignored, and defaults
    set by the template half stand where not overlaid
  No mapped test

Scenario: namespace read failure keeps the defaults
  Given the @Namespace get raises (namespace gone or RBAC)
  When @run catches at the outer block
  Then the warning is logged, no overlay key exists, and the returned map still
    carries use_backup/ha/name from the template half
  No mapped test

Tasks:
  [ ] Cover the scenarios from ./context.sdd's new tenant resolver test harness
      (no tenant hook test ships today).
  [?] The name rewrite erases the `get_tenant_name()` label value (e.g. `acme`
      becomes `team-a`) one slot after it was fetched; the label identity then
      exists nowhere in the final context. Confirm the rewrite is the contract or
      the fetch should move.
  [?] The use_backup re-check is self-referential through the alias: it can fire
      only when an annotation wrote a non-bool, and it then reads back that very
      corrupted slot — a no-op, `false` can never be restored. Decide whether it
      must hold a reference to the minted default (or be dropped).
  [?] Type-trust on the overlay: `vynil.solidite.fr/ha: "\"yes\""` would land a
      string and the `if context.namespace.ha` branch in
      ./../lib/backup_context.rhai fails on a non-bool condition. Decide whether
      overlay values get a type allowlist.

Done when:
  Scenarios mapped through the orchestrator slot, the Task decisions closed, key
    spellings cross-checked against ./context.sdd and
    ./../lib/backup_context.rhai, `specdd lint` green.
